# Lumière Pâtisserie Website

## Project Overview
This is the production website for **Lumière Pâtisserie**, a French patisserie in Canada. The site is deployed via **Railway** and connected to the `main` branch (changes to main go live immediately).

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend:** React + Vite, React Router, CSS Modules, react-spring animations
- **Backend:** Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB, Mongoose (mostly unused - frontend is serverless)
- **Deployment:** Railway (connected to `main` branch)
- **Contact Form:** Google Apps Script (no backend dependency)

## Project Structure
```
Lumiere-web/
├── App/          # React frontend (Vite)
│   └── src/
│       ├── components/
│       ├── pages/
│       └── styles/
└── Backend/      # Express API (mostly unused)
public/
├── products.csv  # Product data (editable spreadsheet)
└── images/       # Optimized product images
```

## Key Features
- Menu page with categorized products (cakes, pastries, bread, bakery shelf)
- Rainbow gradient UI accents, spring animations
- Mobile-responsive with hamburger menu
- CSV-based product management (no code changes needed for product updates)

## Important Files
- `public/products.csv` - Edit prices, descriptions, allergens here
- `CHANGELOG.md` - Document all changes with dates
- `Lumiere-web/App/src/` - Main frontend code

## Branch Strategy
- `main` - Production (auto-deploys to Railway → live website)
- `development` - Safe development branch (work here first)
- Merge to `main` only when ready to go live

## Product Categories
`onebite`, `cakes`, `personal-desserts`, `pastries`, `bread`, `bakery-shelf`

